{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 1 COMPLETE — confirmed parsimonious account and experiments\n\nPrimary defect (already repaired on main, still present in stale Gerrit patchsets): affected 1129/1130/1131/1136 revisions omit 96a0d5c3f and retain unconditional --filter=blob:none followed by read-tree + checkout-index with no up-front blob refill. Exact 1129 code failed the blob-starved no-lazy-fetch oracle with all 40 blobs absent; the same tree with 96a0d5c3f passed. A GIT_TRACE2_EVENT runtime probe on pre-fix code observed 40 git-fetch child starts for 40 files; fixed main passed both the completeness and bounded-fetch oracles. The base fde6 run 30660757264 froze before 1129 tests existed; isolated 1129 tests passed in 1.66s. Runner outage and merely-slow-suite alternatives are rejected. Closed bug 747f and its certified regression contract establish defect legitimacy.\n\nContainment defect: .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml test job has no timeout-minutes, so GitHub applies its 360-minute default. The rerun burst occupied 16 matrix jobs while later run 30676012105 queued, explaining why manual cancellation clears the queue. The workflow documents normal 10–16 minute execution; a 60-minute job bound preserves a >3x macOS margin while eliminating manual-clear dependence. Empirical evidence resolves the code-tracer/historical legitimacy ambiguity in favor of defect.\n\nCaller/dependency sweep: _build-and-test.yml has exactly two callers, test.yml and gerrit-verify.yaml. Both consume the same test job result and benefit from a bounded failure; neither behaviorally depends on six-hour execution. Expected post-fix behavior: every reusable pytest matrix job ends success/failure within 60 minutes, and a blocked worker cannot retain a hosted slot beyond that bound.\n\nPHASE 2 TEST CONTRACT CARD\nauthoritative_contract: user incident requirement that CI not remain manual-clear-dependent; _build-and-test.yml documents 10–16m normal duration; GitHub workflow syntax defines timeout-minutes as the job execution bound and defaults omission to 360m.\ntrigger_preconditions: reusable workflow test job exists and runs the OS/Python matrix.\nproduction_path: parsed .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml jobs.test configuration consumed by both CI callers.\ntest_tier: config-as-artifact unit test; a lower tier cannot validate workflow configuration, and live dispatch is intentionally not authorized.\nobservable_postcondition: jobs.test.timeout-minutes is exactly 60.\nci_gate: default pytest suite / make test.\nnegative_control: omitted — single-point configuration defect.\ngating proof to capture: exact node collected, executed, RED before workflow edit."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785545521409852001,"uuid":"ed6995a2-d7e0-44f1-98f9-4054f6b19402"}